.TH PERMISSION-AUDIT 1 "2026-10-13" "SASD Freeware" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
permission-audit \- list filesystem objects writable by all users
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B permission-audit
.RB [ --include-sticky ]
.RB [ --one-file-system ]
.RB [ --null ]
.I DIRECTORY
.br
.B permission-audit
.RB [ --help | --version ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Reports entries with the other-write mode bit set. Symbolic links are not
followed or reported. World-writable directories with the sticky bit are
excluded unless explicitly requested. Does not inspect ACLs and never
changes permissions.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B --include-sticky
Also list sticky world-writable directories as sticky-directory.
.TP
.B --one-file-system
Do not descend into other devices.
.TP
.B --null
Emit NUL-terminated TYPE, MODE, PATH fields without summary.
.TP
.BR --help , --version
Display help or version.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 scan completed; 1 incomplete scan; 2 usage error; 3 required library missing.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR find (1),
.BR chmod (1),
.BR stat (1)
